What is Electroless Plating?
Electroless Plating is an autocatalytic chemical process used to deposit a coherent layer of metal onto a substrate without the application of electrical current. This technique provides exceptional corrosion resistance, wear protection, and aesthetic enhancement across diverse industrial applications. The unique characteristic of electroless plating lies in its ability to produce uniform deposits with consistent thickness, even on complex geometries and non-conductive surfaces where traditional electroplating methods prove ineffective or impractical for complex components.
